<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian Q3 private wages rise 0.5 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian Q3 private wages rise 0.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Private sector average weekly ordinary time earnings rose 0.5 percent in the three months to August for a rise of 3.4 percent on the year, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>Final data for average weekly ordinary time earnings for adults employed full time was revised to a rise of 1.0 percent, from the preliminary estimate of 0.7 percent, giving an annual rise of 3.8.  </p>
<p>Average weekly ordinary adult earnings (percentage change):</p>
<p>					May 96-Aug 96  Aug 95 - Aug 96</p>
<p>    Seasonally adjusted	    +1.0		  +3.8</p>
<p>    Trend				+1.0		  +3.7</p>
<p>    Unadjusted			 +0.6		  +3.8</p>
<p>Private sector AWOTE</p>
<p>    Seasonally adjusted	    +0.5		  +3.4</p>
<p>    Trend				+0.7		  +3.4</p>
<p>    Unadjusted			 +0.3		  +3.4</p>
<p>	 -- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
